We develop a novel, numerically efficient approach to solving DGLAP equations for single and double parton distribution functions by leveraging Chebyshev interpolation techniques. This method enhances numerical precision with a reduced number of grid points for PDF evolution, achieving improved efficiency. The DPD evolution process utilizes a cost-effective grid-point scheme, enabling the incorporation of two distinct renormalization scales for each parton. The proposed methods account for NNLO DGLAP kernels and flavor matching. The research integrates Chebyshev interpolation into existing parton distribution function tools, such as NNPDF and SHARE, for both PDF and DPD applications. The latter allows for conceptual extensions to existing frameworks. The final model partons are compatible with usual parton distribution functions. The work's source code is publicly available at a specified repository. Additionally, we provide a comprehensive review of all relevant research on Chebyshev interpolation for DGLAP evolution. The research was funded by ANPCyT, MINECO, and ERC contracts. The authors assume all rights to the code and research findings. 

